Robert Lowe wrote:
> 
> Hi!
> 
> I'm running v4.0B and wanted to install the command line and GUI
> utilities for a SWXCR controller.  setld complained that I didn't
> have the C++ shared libraries installed.  I have the 4.0B O/S CDs, but
> the 4.0 associated products CDs, and when I went to install the
> appropriate kit, setld then complained that it wanted OSFBASE400
> installed,  and I have OSFBASE410.  Anything I can do about this, other
> than paying a few hundred dollars for an H kit, which might then have
> even newer versions and require me to upgrade to 4.0D???  ;-)
> 
> -Robert
Not solving your immediate problem (I thought the associated products
kit
normally shipped with the o/s kit) but you might hit a problem I had
when
I updated from D.U. 3.2g to 4.0b. The installation recommended that I 
reinstall the RAID 200 s/ware, but when I tried, it failed. It turns out
that the C++ shared libraries changed the subset name from 3xx to 4xx (
they were called CXXSHRDA3xx and now CXLSHRDA4xx). In the end I hacked
the kit to accept the new name and all was well. Since my RAID 200 kit
was
18 months old, it wasn't surprising that this happened, but I've not yet
been able to get DEC UK to discover what the official solution is. 
Regards,
John Hill
