> How are the DEC clients connected?  This all sounds like network problems,
> not unclean software.  The best thing to do is run snoop (on Solaris)
> and tcpdump (on DEC) and try to look for places where messages are getting
> lost.  The Digital UNIX FAQ has information about setting up tcpdump.
>
> I've also used ping to find network lossage, but pretty much use tcpdump
> exclusively these days.  You can also try FTPing large files to look
> for throughput problems if you're interesting in absolving NFS of blaim.
>
