Hello everyone,

  We have a situation with a DEC 2100 running DU 4.0a running as an NFS
server for a network. It's serving 3 12GB logical volumes over a FDDI
connection to the backbone. The Sun clients are connected 10BaseT hubs
or switches, with the switches having a FDDI connection to the backbone.
Our Sun clients continually have problems with the DEC NFS mounts. We
continually see: 

NFS server alphasrv not responding still trying
NFS server alphasrv ok

 DEC Unix clients work fine. The Sun clients get these errors, and NFS
runs real slow. I have set the NFS version to 2. No help. I have also
done some kernel tuning as suggested by the "System Tuning and
Performance Management" online guide. We have set rsize and wsize to
1024 - no help. The number of nfsiod's has been upped to 32 - no help. I
have changed the kernel parameters - maxusers, somaxconn, sominconn,
pmtu_enabled - all to no avail.

  I am wondering, is there are Sun patch for Sun clients? The problem
seems to point to the Sun NFS client rather than the DEC NFS server. Any
information would be appreciated.


