Gotthard Saghi-Szabo wrote:

> Hi,
>  I would like to know how one can dump remotely AdvFS file systems.
> dump (rdump) does not work with AdvFS, while vdump does not seem to work
> with remote tape devices.
>
> Thanks in advance,
> Gotthard

 just use dd and rsh (Host with tape must be trusted)  :

vdump 0f - domain#fset | rsh host_with_tape dd of=/dev/nrmt0h bs=60k


and to restore

rsh host_with_tape dd if=/dev/nrmt0h bs=60k | (cd where_you_restore ;
vrestore -xf -)

bs=60k, is to have the standard vdump blocksize on your tape, and to be able
to restore it somewhere locally on a system without option.

