Hi,
This depends on what Bull Machines you have. If you have a machine of the
DPX/20, Escala or Estrella series, the operating system is AIX (coming
from IBM, some Bull enhancements for hardware components or
telecommunications) from version 3.2.5 to 4.3. Most of the DPX/20 and
Escala are IBM RS6000 (common production), some of the Estrellas are
Motorola machines (with PowerPC 6xx, PCI bus).

If you are talking about old machines as DPX/2, the operating system is
BOS which is a Bull dialect based on System V with BSD enhancements.

I hope you are not having even older types like DPX/2000 or Questar 700.
Here the operating system is SPIX, also a System V dialect.

Regards

Helmut Leininger
