Gotthard Saghi-Szabo wrote:
> 
> Hi,
>  I would like to know how one can dump remotely AdvFS file systems.
> dump (rdump) does not work with AdvFS, while vdump does not seem to work
> with remote tape devices.

Mentioned prior, is the way with rsh (I didn't think of that, a good
point).

Another way (which I have used) is via NFS. Command vdump can backup ANY
system-recognised FS type. You can backup UFS, AdvFS, NFS, anything.
That is because vdump/vrestore works on MOUNTED file systems only.

The proper procedure is to create a clone of the file-set you wish to
backup, export it through NFS. Than mount it on the HOST_WITH_TAPE and
do the vdump. The only setback is that the HOST_WITH_TAPE must be
Digital UNIX, appropriate version.

All in all, the procedure with rsh should be beter. This is an
alternative.

Nix.





