AHA, I found the answer to my problems through careful reading of the
security html documentation. I discovered that I needed to add the line

auth=local,yp

to the file /etc/svc.conf. Stupidly, the secsetup script doesn't do this.
This makes the user authentication search both local and NIS protected
password databases. The documentation also says it's important not to have
a password entry in both the local and the NIS databases, because some
utilities will change only the NIS passwords, whereas others (such as
logging in) will use the first database entry that matches, leading to
inconsistent results (at least for the recommended local,yp ordering show above.)

- David Potterveld
