shay_tochner@magic-sw.com wrote:
> I installed Digital-Unix 4.0d ...
> The cde starts and works normally on the console (graphic) ...
> On the Xterminals ... I get the message:Faal error: XDM session declined.

You may need to 'add' your X-terminals to the devassign and ttys databases. 
If you are using C2 security then use the commands

echo '*\:*:v_type=xdisplay:chkent:' | /tcb/bin/edauth -s -dv
echo '*\:*:t_devname=*\:*:t_login_timeout#0:t_xdisplay:chkent:' | /tcb/bin/edauth -s -dt

If you are at base security then you may need to manually edit the files
/etc/auth/system/devassign and /etc/auth/system/ttys (instead of the above
edauth commands).

