Stephen Leake wrote:

> Rob Kirkbride wrote (in small part:
> > The problem is you don't seem to
> > be able to use realtime priorities any more from Ada as it assumes
> > process scope when creating the threads which is a little annoying to
> > have this changed on us. I realise in C you can change this option.
>
> If you can change it in C, you can change it in Ada; just import the
> routine and call it! If you have to call it before the Ada environment
> task is created, then you'll have to write a main wrapper in C that
> calls the Ada elaboration and finalization code. Either way, it should
> be doable.
>
> --
> - Stephe

 Just a reminder -- in Digital UNIX 4.0-4.0C, all pthreads
are process-scope threads. The only exception is for programs linked
statically on pre-V4.0 versions of the OS. Only in V4.0D was
system-contention scope (re)introduced. So, for a system
scope (bound) thread, the priority/policy changes will again affect the
thread's systemwide scheduling behavior.
If you're not doing realtime, you should stick with
process-scope threads (right, Dave?).

Jeff
