ADA = Americans with Disabilities Act. Most of the tricks to make a web
page useable by all browsers are the same tricks to make a web page ADA
compliant. Basically, a blind person needs to be able to read a web
page. This is usually done through a text-only browser and a reader
(speech synthesizer). They rely on responsible HTML authors to include
things such as ALT tags and extra code for imagemaps, javascripts, etc.
