On Wed, 18 Mar 1998 14:35:24 GMT, not.me@a.b.com (John Sheldrake)
wrote:
>ls -als /dev/pty* | wc -l gives 48 but we still get the message when
>only 32 users are logged in.
>Does anybody know what I've missed??

I'm assuming you're using 4.0 here:
Have you checked your /etc/sysconfigtab file?

In there is a section specifying the number of ptys available . it
looks like this:

ptys:
<tab>nptys = 512

will give you 512 pseudo-terminals.

If you're running 3.x check out your kernel config, You'll need a line
like:

pseudo-device    	rpty      512

to give 512 pseudo-terminals. Obviously you'll need to re-compile the
kernel.

Finally, if it's none of the above, make sure yopu have no "gaps" in
the device numbers. They should start at ttyp0, then q, r, s, t ...
etc. If the "r" series is missing you'll also get the problem you've
got.

Hope this helps,



