You NEED the "307" library or later (there is a "308" library now for
Unix 3.2<x>).
Navigator 4.04 must have been built with DEC C++ 5.3 or later which
requires the "307" or
later runtime libraries.

You can get the required library from:

ftp://ftp.digital.com/public/osf/v3.2c/c++/class/cxxchrdae01308.tar

Unpack the tar file in a temporary directory. Use "setld -d" to
uninstall the current C++ runtime
libraries, then use "setld -l" to install these updated ones. They are
upwards compatible with the old ones.

You only need this for Unix 3.2<x>.  There is not problem with Digital
Unix 4.0 or later.

