>Alpha 433 Workstation

Are you REALLY sure you want to do this ?

If your machine is connected to a network, anyone who can telnet to your
machine is potentially able to log in as root - that security feature is
there for a good reason !

If your account is in the "system" group, you can su to root once you
have logged in to your account.

If you don't want to put your account into the "system" group, use
something like "sudo".

Either alternative is safer than adding the list of ptys to
/etc/securettys !

Chris
