"Vincent Huang" <vincent9@ms3.hinet.net> writes:

> So,here is my question , I want to copy some files from original
> harddisk 1, How sould I do to mount original harddisk 1 to
> other mount point..and I can copy files from that place..?

You didn't say which version of the os you are using, but with
4.0d you can use the 'mount -o dual' option to mount a copy of
a fileset while one is already mounted.

cd /etc/fdmns
mkdir old_root; cd old_root; ln -s /dev/rz1a; cd ..
mkdir old_usr; cd old_usr; ln -s /dev/rz1g; cd ..
mkdir old_var; cd old_var; ln -s /dev/rz1h; cd ..

mount -o dual old_usr#usr /mnt

and so on.

