/dev/rz0g refers to partition "g" for the disk at SCSI ID 0. DEC (like
for instance SunOS) uses letters "a" to "h" to refer to the 8 possible
partitions on a disk. The command

disklabel -r rz0

will give you the full details about the disk at SCSI ID 0 (including
partition information).
Regards,
John Hill
 
