From: Jeff Sullivan <jps@zk3.dec.com>
Subject: Re: Templates in digital C++
Date: 1998/03/11
Message-ID: <3506EC12.38A8A650@zk3.dec.com>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 333080367
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
References: <34F2D7A3.41C6@bev.net>
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
Organization: Digital Equipment Corporation
Mime-Version: 1.0
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1


This issue was handled offline, but I am posting the resolution
here so that it may help others. The answer came from someone
else in the C++ group who worked the issue with Chris...

The problem turned out to be that Chris had a source
and include hierarchy in his application. Digital's template
automatic instantiation scheme requires that the
template repository files get created in a directory or
directories so that the final link can know where they are.

Once the makefile was changed to use the -ptr option
to specify the complete path name of where all the
template repository files should go and -I flags were added so
that the pre-linker could find the relevant include files,
the application compiled and linked successfully.

For any Digital C++ users with similar problems, Section 
5.2.9.2 "Building an Application" from the DEC C++ Version 
5.6 Using Guide covers this topic.

-Jeff
