Programs that exhibit erratic behaviour are more likely to have
a subscript error.

The request for automatic storage for 6 arrays of
size 1234 each cannot be considered to be demanding.

Your program uses assumed size dummy arrays for subroutine
"name" (x, a, b)
rather than assumed shape arrays.  Subscript checking is
not generally carried our for assumed size arrays, whereas
it usully can be requested and applied for assumed shape.

Have you considered substituting assumed shape
arrays and turning on subscript checking?



