Peter,

Firstly, you have to make sure your have the lastest patches installed. The lastest patch
for Digital UNIX is BL8 release on Dec/97.  It include some of the performance improvement
on NFS and VM.

Secondly, you can uses "ps aux" command to monitor the system and find out
which process occupy most of the CPU time and memory resource.

Also, UNIX 4.0x by default will uses NFS Version 3 to mount the NFS file
system, if failed then will try NFSV2. So if you have mixed enviroment, you
should specify which is V2 and which is V3.

Good Luck!

David Lee.

