> 
> Colin Carpenter.

If you can get stuff from DAT to a UNIX, then you have a number of
options.

1. FTP: good for casual file transfers. Works fine, see man pages.
2. rcp - Remote CoPy: good for steady copying.
   If you'll have this need for copying files all the time.
   Takes some time to configure and is a potencial security hole.
3. scp - Secure CoPy: based on SSh.
4. NFS: this is for something even more steady than rcp.

Cheers,
Nix





