The C++ runtime libraries were an optionally installed Subset
in Unix 3.2<x>. They were on one of the OS CD's, along with the
FORTRAN, COBOL and ADA RTLs. I don't know which one offhand.

I think this is the one you want:

CXXSHRDA307     DEC C++ Class Library, Run-Time Support

This subset includes:
% setld -i CXXSHRDA307
./usr/lib/cmplrs/cxx/CXXSHRDA.Links
./usr/lib/cmplrs/cxx/libcomplex.so
./usr/lib/cmplrs/cxx/libcxx.so
./usr/lib/cmplrs/cxx/libtask.so
./usr/lib/nls/msg/en_US.ISO8859-1/cxxl.cat

    
In Unix 4.0, the C++ Runtime libraries are part of OSFBASE.

Hope it helps,
-Jeff

